      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case of a young female with an acute idiopathic low cerebrospinal fluid pressure is presented. Clinical-imaging manifestations were typical and two consecutive blood patches resulted in a complete and durable resolution of the symptomatology. We present a review of the various investigation and therapeutic techniques."},
